# Kor, Cause of Vengeance: with no other creature, "another creature" has nothing to offer (CR 109.5, 701.21a), so Bot1
# is not asked and nothing is drawn or pumped. Kor itself would match the attack trigger, which is exactly what
# "another" excludes, and it is still 4/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Kor, Cause of Vengeance
Black Lotus x4
Black Lotus x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Cast(Spend: B, B, R, W)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Kor, Cause of Vengeance > Bot2)
# Nothing is asked: Kor is the only creature and "another creature" excludes it, which the damage below shows - the
# script runs straight through combat to the end.
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 4
Bot2.Life = 16
